     "rate": "+0%",
     "text": "A five year old typed PRINT HELLO WORLD into a monochrome terminal in nineteen ninety nine. Dartmouth College introduced BASIC in nineteen sixty four to make programming simple for beginners. By nineteen eighty two, Commodore sixty four systems booted BASIC directly from hardware ROM. Starting in kindergarten feels like a shortcut to building digital empires before age thirty. Then rapid innovation changed everything. Brendan Eich created JavaScript in ten days in nineteen ninety five. By twenty twenty, developer Anthony Fu built Vite Plugin Inspector to map complex browser elements back to editor source code. Twenty five years of shifting tools turns early prodigies into full time syntax unlearners. Code moves faster than human memory."
